{"G1457":{"id":"G1457","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G1457","disambiguated_id":"G1457 =","unique_id":"G1457","headword":"ἐγκαινίζω","transliteration":"egkainizō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to inaugurate","definition_en":"ἐγκαινίζω, see: ἐνκ-.\n ἐν-καινίζω (Rec. ἐγκ-, see: ἐν), \n [in LXX: (to renew) 1Ki.11:14, 2Ch.15:8, Ps 50(51):10 (Br-m pi.); (to dedicate) Deu.20:5, 2Ch.7:5 (-^jn); Isa.16:11 41:1 45:16 (aliter in Heb.), Si 33(36):6, 1Ma.4:36,54,57 5:1, 2Ma.2:29 *;] \n1. to innovate (Eust.). 2. to renew (LXX ut supr.). 3. to initiate, inaugurate, dedicate (LXX ut supr.) : διαθήκην, Heb.9:18 ; ὁδόν, ib. 10:20 (Cremer, 323).†\n (AS)","source_line":1589}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"foi-inaugurada","count":1},{"gloss":"consagrado","count":1}]},"G2000":{"id":"G2000","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2000","disambiguated_id":"G2000 =","unique_id":"G2000","headword":"ἐπισφαλής","transliteration":"episphalēs","lexical_morphology":"G:A","gloss_en":"dangerous/unsteady","definition_en":"ἐπισφαλής, -ές\n (σφάλλω, to cause to full), [in LXX: Wis.9:14 (cf. -ῶς, Wis.4:4) * ;] \n__1. prone to fall (Plat.). \n __2. dangerous (Hipp., Plut., al.): Act.27:9.†\n (AS)","source_line":2141}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"perigosa","count":1}]},"G2134":{"id":"G2134","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G2134","disambiguated_id":"G2134 =","unique_id":"G2134","headword":"εὐνουχίζω","transliteration":"eunouchizō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to become a eunuch","definition_en":"εὐνουχίζω\n (εὐνοῦχος), \nto make a eunuch of, castrate: pass., Mat.19:12; metaphorically, εὐ. έαυτόν, ib.†\n (AS)","source_line":2276}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"castrados","count":1},{"gloss":"castraram","count":1}]},"G339":{"id":"G339","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G0339","disambiguated_id":"G0339 =","unique_id":"G0339","headword":"ἀνακαθίζω","transliteration":"anakathizō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to sit up","definition_en":"ἀνα-καθ-ίζω\n (see: καθίζω); \n __1. trans., to set up. \n __2. Intrans., to sit up: Luk.7:15 (WH, mg., ἐκάθισεν), Act.9:40 (frequently in medical writings: MM, VGT, see word).\n † (AS)","source_line":443}],"occurrence_count":2,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"sentou","count":2}]},"G3669":{"id":"G3669","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3669","disambiguated_id":"G3669 =","unique_id":"G3669","headword":"ὁμοίωσις","transliteration":"homoiōsis","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"likeness","definition_en":"ὁμοίωσις, -εως, ἡ\n (ὁμοιόω) [in LXX chiefly for דְּמוּת, Psa.58:4, al. ;] \n__1. a making like, becoming like (Plat.). \n __2. likeness: Jas.3:9 (LXX).† \n SYN.: see: ὁμοίωμα, and cf. Tr., Syn., § xv (AS)","source_line":3785}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"semelhança","count":1}]},"G3831":{"id":"G3831","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3831","disambiguated_id":"G3831 =","unique_id":"G3831","headword":"πανήγυρις","transliteration":"panēguris","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"assembly","definition_en":"πανήγυρις, -εως, ἡ\n (πᾶς + ἄγυρας = ἀγορά), [in LXX: Hos.2:11(13) 9:5, Eze.46:11 (מוֹעֵד), Amo.5:21 (עֲצָרָה) * ;] \nprop., a national festal assembly in honour of a god; hence, generally, any festal assembly: Heb.12:23 (for exx. in π., see MM, xviii).†\n SYN.: ἐκκλησία (which see), συναγωγή (AS)","source_line":3949}],"occurrence_count":1,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"reunião-em-massa","count":1}]},"G4359":{"id":"G4359","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G4359","disambiguated_id":"G4359 =","unique_id":"G4359","headword":"προσοφείλω","transliteration":"prosopheilō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to owe besides","definition_en":"to owe besides or still , (Thucydides): absolute, προσοφείλοντας ἡμᾶς ἐνέγραψεν (Demosthenes Orator):—;Pass. to be still owing, be still due , (Thucydides); so, ἡ ἔχθρ